entry.summary:
Astro, the meta-framework JAMStack and Next alternative thanks to its "islands architecture", recommends to use Zod to define a data schema. So far, so good. It works well in Astro components, and it works in React when I define the same schema redundantly.
Zod:
// content.config.ts (Zod)
icon: z.enum(['book', 'blogpost']).default('book').optional(),

React:
// Book.tsx (TypeScript JSX)
interface CardProps {
  icon?: 'book'|'blogpost';

Surely there must be a way to infer the interface from Zod, but I didn't find it in the documentation. Claude and Perplexity claim that it works and that it's documented, but fail to point to an authoritative documentation link for that specific use case, and they turn around in circles suggesting variations of hallucinated code that never completely works …
